I guess as much as launguage is a barier to getting some of these shows out to like different places around the world really it's China that a lot of film and TV studios are trying to work with next

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:09.640
I mean they've been doing it for a long time but because China's cinema is state controlled they only allow I think it's about 20 foreign films in per year

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:15.980
And that short list of films includes big blockbusters like Star Wars, Avengers: Age of Ultron, Captain America: Civil War

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.680
So if you're a film studio and you want your film to make money you know you obviously release it in as many countries as possible

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.940
But there's a billion people in China, that's a lot of people that could buy a lot of movie tickets

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.000
So if you can get in into China it's a big deal

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:35.780
Which is why sometimes they make HUGE edits to the film because China is really specific about stuff they allow in the country

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:42.040
Like ghost stories is a really good example of something that they hate. Their government really does not like supernatural stories

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.740
So if you lived in China and you wanted to see one, you would probably have to pirate it

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.180
